Bdynamic
Driver Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_NORMAL)

Bstatic
Driver Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_NORMAL)

Xbind-lazy
Driver Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_NORMAL)

Xbind-now
Driver Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_NORMAL)

; Kept out of the shared target_flags word deliberately.  target_flags is one
; 32-bit int for a whole back end, and this file is included by every port that
; has a VxWorks configuration.  In a single-target build that costs nothing --
; only one OS's .opt files are ever read.  In a build configured for many
; triples of one back end, every OS that back end supports contributes its
; masks at once, and for i386 that is exactly one bit too many: 33 target_flags
; masks, which opth-gen.awk reports as `#error too many target masks'.
; Nothing outside this file names MASK_VXWORKS_RTP -- every user goes through
; TARGET_VXWORKS_RTP, which opth-gen defines the same way either way -- so
; giving the bit a variable of its own is invisible to the ports.
TargetVariable
int vxworks_flags

mrtp
Target RejectNegative Mask(VXWORKS_RTP) Var(vxworks_flags) Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_NORMAL)
Assume the VxWorks RTP environment.

; VxWorks AE has two modes: kernel mode and vThreads mode.  In
; general, back ends do not actually need to know which mode they're
; in, so we do not have to set any flags.
mvthreads
Target RejectNegative Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_AE)
Assume the VxWorks vThreads environment.

non-static
Driver Condition(VXWORKS_KIND == VXWORKS_KIND_NORMAL)
